hoardDB certification summary (perf-record/2)
CAVEAT (1) These guests complete a synced 4 KiB write in 3.6 to 4.3 ms, about 250 syncs a second; replicated hoardDB and MySQL pay two sequential syncs before the acknowledgement (owner, then replica), MongoDB journals on the members in parallel; none of it transfers to local NVMe, where a sync costs tens of microseconds.
CAVEAT (2) The virtual disk's write-back caching behaviour was not verified.
CAVEAT (3) The host has a hybrid-core CPU; its effect is visible only through the canary.
CAVEAT (4) The fsync sidecar adds one synced write per second per server VM.
CAVEAT (5) The development database that calibrates 16.4 is a development database.
LIMITATION same-vm-repeats: the median of three is of back-to-back repeats on one VM (no engine-to-VM rotation); a slow guest is not separated from the engine. Applies to: C1/hoarddb, C1/mongo.

